To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 2 other than $a_{24}=2$ equal to $0.$

To do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:

$$
\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 & -6 \\ -10 & 4 & 6 & 2 \\ 4 & 3 & -8 & 8 \\ 6 & -8 & -1 & 1\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}+5C_{4}}\begin{bmatrix}-37 & 4 & 7 & -6 \\ 0 & 4 & 6 & 2 \\ 44 & 3 & -8 & 8 \\ 11 & -8 & -1 & 1\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-2C_{4}}\begin{bmatrix}-37 & 16 & 7 & -6 \\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 2 \\ 44 & -13 & -8 & 8 \\ 11 & -10 & -1 & 1\end{bmatrix}
\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}-3C_{4}}\begin{bmatrix}-37 & 16 & 25 & -6 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\ 44 & -13 & -32 & 8 \\ 11 & -10 & -4 & 1\end{bmatrix}=B
$$

Therefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are

$C_{2}:=C_{2}-2C_{4}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}-3C_{4}$.
